--- Rosetta Code: Executable library
--- https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Executable_library
--- The second executable. The library is executable_library_hailstone.co, which
--- lies beside this file: `use` imports it in the standard manner, and only its
--- declarations come in (its own top-level lines, the library's command-line
--- part, run only when that file is run itself). No setup: `crow run
--- executable_library.co` reads the library's source, and `crow build` makes one
--- binary of the two. Here the library's hailstone finds the sequence length
--- that occurs most often for 1 <= n < 100,000.
use executable_library_hailstone as library

lengths = for n in range[1, 100000]
    len[library.hailstone[n]]

--- how many starting numbers give each length
counts = map[]
for length in lengths
    if length in counts
        counts = set[counts, length, counts[length] + 1]
    else
        counts = set[counts, length, 1]

common = 0
for length in keys[counts]
    if common eq 0 or counts[length] gt counts[common]
        common = length
log['The hailstone length returned most often for 1 <= n < 100,000 is `common`, by `counts[common]` numbers']
